{"id": "EUVD-2026-59487", "enisaUuid": "a883e1e6-8c08-3cd2-94b0-20c4ff41b9f1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wcn36xx: fix OOB read from firmware count in PRINT_REG_INFO indication\n\nThe firmware-controlled rsp->count field is used as the loop bound for\nindexing into the flexible rsp->regs[] array without validation against\nthe message length. A count exceeding the actual data causes out-of-\nbounds reads from the heap-allocated message buffer.\n\nAdd a check that count fits within the received message.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:34", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22b0b8572a64362531dd0ed499b75e16282aeb2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3cf92b44c4fb88a5e8de8733a4494c0956606bca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0907c06dccae9e3c8d5a68eb9014beec73a36e79", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64228dfc4247aca178c01e5a37af7d8dcc7a6089", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23d210877968657bd07e1a517e0b516db20a1d80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f03782f7f41f2afee5076a1ef08ced5649218771", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f987efff29a5fe45320ea5991c9d5cb98b676953", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/df2187acfca6c6cca372c5d35f42394d9c270b09"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9fwg-3fvg-fm8h", "CVE-2026-74340"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00bb76d9-bc46-3da7-8d05-509eda91cfdf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43efa3c0f241e04862be8e6a68ff765d36cde1ba <df2187acfca6c6cca372c5d35f42394d9c270b09"}, {"id": "0b401baa-ecb5-34f0-b725-369f36ecbbe8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "14279ea8-50b1-3a97-9ec3-0b062085c244", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "43efa3c0f241e04862be